WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:04.900
You can't please everyone, and that goes double
for people who consider themselves to be hardcore

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.760
Disney fans.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.400
More than a few Disney die-hards are up in
arms on Twitter over the trailer for the upcoming

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.280
live-action remake of Mulan, which will not
be a musical and will exclude a couple of

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.200
key characters.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:21.760
The beloved 1998 animated original centered
on Fa Mulan, a peasant girl who disguises

00:00:21.769 --> 00:00:26.330
herself as a man so that she can enlist in
the Chinese army, in place of her ailing father,

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:28.800
to help defend her country against the marauding
Huns.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.760
At her side on her journey is Mushu, a tiny,
wisecracking dragon who hopes to restore his

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:38.840
tarnished honor by helping Mulan succeed — a
task made more difficult by General Li Shang,

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.100
who serves as an antagonist for much of the
film before being won over by Mulan's bravery

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.100
and cleverness.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.000
Shang and Mushu are the characters at the
center of the Twitter uproar, as it's been

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.060
revealed that neither will appear in the live-action
film — a revelation that didn't sit well

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.500
with legions of passionate fans of the original.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.460
"They'll be begging me to come back to work!"

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.680
This isn't to say that many of these fans
are going to refrain from buying a ticket.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:05.080
Disgruntled fans still rage-attending movies
is a common theme among the outpouring of

00:01:05.080 --> 00:01:10.180
angry tweets, as illustrated by a tweet from
user @_dearwallflower, who acknowledged that

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:14.000
the version of Mulan featured in the trailer
looks remarkably badass, saying,

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:17.420
"This is the Mulan we obviously wanted, but
Mushu?

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:18.200
Li-Shang?

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:18.920
Music?

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:23.020
I mean, imma go see it regardless, but imma
also be sad."

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.810
The sentiment was echoed by user @GoodyButts,
who ran down her complete list of reactions

00:01:27.810 --> 00:01:28.940
to the trailer in her tweet:

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:33.619
"Cries watching the #Mulan trailer… listens
to "I'll Make A Man Out of You"… remembers

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:36.860
there won't be musical numbers or Mushu…
cries some more…

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:38.580
REMAINS EXCITED FOR THIS MOVIE."

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:43.859
One user even flat-out stated that they were
predisposed to rage at the idea of a non-musical

00:01:43.859 --> 00:01:47.409
version of Mulan, but that the trailer pretty
much won them over, saying,

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.719
"I wanna HATE the Mulan remake but the way
she twiddles her sword with her hair flowing

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:52.220
in the wind?

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:53.900
It looks god tier."

00:01:54.249 --> 00:02:00.180
Meanwhile, user @MikeMcdonaldii pointed out
that it's unrealistic to expect the same movie.

00:02:00.189 --> 00:02:05.819
"So y'all mad that Disney live-action remakes
are just shot 4 shot w/ the animated movies

00:02:05.819 --> 00:02:10.500
but y'all mad that this #Mulan has it own
vision from its animated counterpart."

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.700
He has a heck of a point.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:16.520
This May's live-action version of Aladdin,
although it raked in nearly a billion dollars

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.810
in worldwide box office receipts, has been
called out by fans and critics alike for being

00:02:20.810 --> 00:02:25.280
a by-the-numbers recreation of the original
that doesn't bother to carve out its own unique

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:25.780
vision.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:30.880
The same complaints have been leveled preemptively
at The Lion King, which uses CGI to render

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.480
its characters in live action.

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.200
Of course, The Lion King has been blowing
away preview audiences, so it may prove to

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:41.230
be the film that pokes king-sized holes in
those way-too-early criticisms.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:45.830
Conversely, Tim Burton's recent remake of
Dumbo drew fire for deviating too much from

00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:46.840
the original's story.

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:51.060
Ultimately, that film was among the least
successful of the Mouse House's live-action

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:52.980
reimaginings of their classic library.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:58.880
It's almost as if the Disney faithful simply
have no idea what exactly they want from these

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:02.990
remakes, before or after they've been released,
although that doesn't seem to stop them from

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:03.840
purchasing tickets.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.960
With only the one teaser trailer to go on,
Mulan's creative team appears to be on the

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:08.620
right track.

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:14.200
Actress Yifei Liu looks awesome in the title
role, and the original movie based on an ancient

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.930
Chinese legend tells a complex story with
themes relevant to our times, one that will

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:24.320
lend itself well to a more serious treatment
without singing, dancing, and talking dragons.

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:26.060
“You just say the word and I'm there.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:26.800
Mushu…

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.940
And let me say something.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:32.660
Anyone who's foolish enough to threaten our
family, vengeance will be mine."

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.320
The flick hits theaters on March 27th, 2020.

